    <!-- LOCAL IMPACT TRACK -->
    <section class="section" id="local-impact">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header reveal">
          <div class="section-eyebrow">// TRACK · LOCAL IMPACT</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Build for <span class="text-accent">Ann Arbor.</span></h2>
          <p class="section-sub">a2Tech360 spends ten days celebrating what this region invents. This is the part where we invent something.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="a2g-li reveal">
          <div class="a2g-li-prompt">
            <span class="a2g-li-tag">★ THE PROMPT</span>
            <p class="a2g-li-quote">Build something that makes life <em>measurably better</em> for people in Ann Arbor and Washtenaw County.</p>
            <p class="a2g-li-body">Every problem worth solving here already belongs to somebody. Riders waiting on a route that doesn't quite work. Small businesses competing against everything online. Nonprofits doing serious work on thin budgets. Students, newcomers, parents, makers, and longtime residents who could help each other if they knew how.</p>
            <p class="a2g-li-body">Pick one of theirs. Pick something we haven't thought of. The only requirement is that <b>a specific person in this county could use what you build on Monday morning.</b></p>
            <div class="a2g-li-rule">
              <span class="a2g-li-rule-tag">ONE RULE</span>
              <p>Ground it in something real. Talk to someone who has the problem. Judges will ask who you built this for, and &ldquo;everyone&rdquo; is the wrong answer.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="a2g-li-side">
            <div class="a2g-li-dirs-label">A few directions, not a menu</div>
            <div class="a2g-li-dirs">
              <div class="a2g-li-dir"><span class="a2g-li-dir-icon">🚌</span><b>Getting around</b><p>Transit, parking, biking, and the last mile between where people are and where they need to be.</p></div>
              <div class="a2g-li-dir"><span class="a2g-li-dir-icon">🏪</span><b>Main Street</b><p>Helping local businesses reach the people already walking past them.</p></div>
              <div class="a2g-li-dir"><span class="a2g-li-dir-icon">🤝</span><b>Showing up</b><p>Connecting volunteers, mentors, and donors to the organizations that need them.</p></div>
              <div class="a2g-li-dir"><span class="a2g-li-dir-icon">🏠</span><b>Access</b><p>Food, housing, benefits, childcare, and the gap between a service existing and someone finding it.</p></div>
              <div class="a2g-li-dir"><span class="a2g-li-dir-icon">🏛️</span><b>Civic clarity</b><p>Making local data, meetings, permits, and decisions legible to normal humans.</p></div>
              <div class="a2g-li-dir"><span class="a2g-li-dir-icon">🌳</span><b>Belonging</b><p>Helping people find each other and find what's happening.</p></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="a2g-li-foot reveal">
          <div class="a2g-li-card">
            <div class="sfg-checklist-title">BUILD REQUIREMENTS</div>
            <p>Projects build on the <b>Jaseci/Jac stack</b> (per event-wide requirements) and may incorporate <b>Google or IBM tooling</b> alongside it. All teams must run their code through <b>Baz</b> for code review as part of the build process.</p>
            <p class="a2g-li-note">No prior experience with any of this is required. Workshops and mentors will be on site.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="a2g-li-card a2g-li-card-hot">
            <div class="sfg-checklist-title">HOW IT'S JUDGED</div>
            <p>The <b>Grand Prize</b> goes to the team whose project best combines local relevance, technical execution, and a plausible path to existing after the weekend.</p>
            <p class="a2g-li-note">Plus the <b>Community Favorite</b>: every participant votes, and this one belongs to the room.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="a2g-li-close reveal">You do not need to be a professional engineer. You do not need a team when you arrive. <b>You do need to care about this place.</b></p>
      </div>
    </section>

