            <div class="section-eyebrow">// GETTING THERE</div>
            <h2 class="sfg-h3">Leinweber, on North Campus</h2>
            <p class="sfg-body">JacHacks A2Tech takes place at the Leinweber Computer Science and Information Building, <b>2200 Hayward Street, Ann Arbor, MI 48109</b>, on the University of Michigan's North Campus. Volunteers and organizers will be around all weekend to point you in the right direction. Look for the JacHacks signage when you arrive.</p>
            <div class="sfg-transit">
              <div class="sfg-transit-item">
                <span class="sfg-transit-tag">THERIDE</span>
                <p>TheRide operates Ann Arbor's local bus network. For North Campus, use the U-M North Campus routes and check current schedules before traveling; routes and arrival times can change.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="sfg-transit-item">
                <span class="sfg-transit-tag">M-BUS</span>
                <p>Take UMich's M-Bus from Central Campus to North via Commuter North, Bursley-Baits, or Northwood.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="sfg-transit-item">
                <span class="sfg-transit-tag">FROM DTW</span>
                <p>The Michigan Flyer runs frequent daily service from Detroit Metro Airport to 500 E. Washington Street in Ann Arbor; from there, take an Ann Arbor bus, rideshare, or taxi to Leinweber. Reserve a seat before traveling. By Uber or Lyft, DTW to Leinweber is typically 30–45 minutes.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="sfg-transit-item">
                <span class="sfg-transit-tag">PARKING</span>
                <p>Visitor parking is in <b>NC48</b> at 2100 Hayward Street, next to Leinweber. Accessible visitor parking is in <b>NC27</b>, entered from Murfin Avenue just south of Hayward. Card-only through AimsMobilePay.com; check posted signs and U-M parking rules.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="sfg-transit-item">
                <span class="sfg-transit-tag">RIDESHARE</span>
                <p>Drop pin: "Leinweber Computer Science and Information Building, 2200 Hayward Street." Use the Hayward Street entrance and follow event signage.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
